    "description": "Oblic quotes, also called backticks, `` \\` `` were used to make a shell call to the operating system. They are deprecated since version 8.5, and they have no more specific usage.\n\n`` \\` `` is a character, that needs to be balanced, when used in code syntax.\n",
    "code": "<?php\n\n    echo `ls -hla`;\n    \n    // moder alternative\n    echo shell_exec('ls -hla');\n\n?>",
